# Genesis Error: Test-Until-Working Rule

## Core rule

**Test in the console again and again until the exe opens properly and all new tools function.**

Never mark work complete until the full verification cycle passes.

## Mandatory verification sequence

Run these steps **before** considering any exe/shortcut/build work done:

1. **Build**: `npm run build:all`
2. **Sync check**: `npm run check-sync` — must show "All versions synchronized"
3. **Launch exe**: `dist-electron\GenesisError.exe` — window must open (no ERR_NOT_FOUND)
4. **Verify tools**: In-app self-check for orbits; view projections; time scale controls

## What to verify

| Check | How |
|-------|-----|
| Exe opens | Genesis Error window appears, no error dialog |
| Multi-planet orbits | Add star + planets, start sim, orbits move |
| View projections | ◇ ⬆ ▬ ◐ buttons switch camera |
| Time scale | Slider responds; FPS stays smooth |
| Sync status | `npm run check-sync` passes |

## If something fails

1. Close all Genesis Error processes
2. Run `npm run build:all` again (from a normal terminal if electron-builder gets EPERM) (from a normal terminal; sandbox may cause electron-builder EPERM)
3. Retry the verification sequence
4. Fix root cause before delivering

## Integration with other rules

- **exe-shortcut-sync**: Version coordination must pass before testing
- **rebuild-preliminaries**: Run `npm install` before `build:all` when needed
